  "body": "HTML specification refers to character encoding as \"character encoding\" instead of simply \"encoding\". Although the intent to disambiguate \"character encoding\" from other kinds of encodings is understandable, it creates a confusion, when a reference is made to the Document object in DOM which has `encoding` field, but no `character encoding` field.\n\nThere's no need to redefine that unspecified \"encoding\" means \"character encoding\" in most cases, as all specifications refer to \"character encoding\" simply as \"encoding\", beginning with the Encoding specification. If there is a need to specifically call \"encoding\" as a \"character encoding\", this can be done with an additional \"character\" word outside the cross-referenced part of the phrase.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13327/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 5:16 PM UTC (de44a77)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13327/2a4e786...de44a77/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 5:16 PM UTC (de44a77)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13327/document-lifecycle.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 5:16 PM UTC (de44a77)\">/document-lifecycle.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13327/2a4e786...de44a77/document-lifecycle.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 5:16 PM UTC (de44a77)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13327/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 5:16 PM UTC (de44a77)\